7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,7\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296753 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296939 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1068 #edb/ref 17592186297063 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1068 #edb/ref 17592186297106 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1069 "q-316617" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1071 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=1,$ and ${x}_{3}=2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1072 #uuid "6e967f50-e84b-5701-ba55-e33a7635ef69" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297526 1074 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=1,$ and ${x}_{3}=2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-(-4))(x-1)(x-2) \\\\  & =3(x+4)(x-1)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+4)(x-1)(x-2) & =3({x}^{2}+3x-4)(x-2) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-6x-4x+8) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-10x+8) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-30x+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-30x+24.$" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296703 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296785 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296829 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1068 #edb/ref 17592186297030 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1069 "q-316619" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1071 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=-3,$ and ${x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1072 #uuid "0160ce9e-9e81-50aa-b03f-bdd233b46397" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297527 1074 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=-3,$ and ${x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-1)(x-(-3))(x-4) \\\\  & =5(x-1)(x+3)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-1)(x+3)(x-4) & =5({x}^{2}+2x-3)(x-4) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-8x-3x+12) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-11x+12) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-55x+60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-55x+60.$" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296657 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296664 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296816 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186297036 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297528 1069 "q-316621" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297528 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297528 1071 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-4,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" 13194139533411 17592186045585 true] [17592186297528 1072 #uuid "5a